      {
        "id": 32,
        "code": "## Padrão 4: Recursão Mútua (Mutual Recursion)\n\nA recursão mútua ocorre quando dois ou mais predicados chamam uns aos outros em um ciclo.\n\n### Exemplo: Par (Even) e Ímpar (Odd)",
        "type": "markdown",
        "language": "markdown",
        "name": "",
        "lastOutput": "",
        "lastOutputHtml": ""
      },
      {
        "id": 33,
        "code": "% Definir is_even e is_odd com recursão mútua\n:- dynamic is_even/1.\n:- dynamic is_odd/1.\n\n% Caso base de is_even\nis_even(0).\n\n% is_even recursivo: N é par se N-1 é ímpar\nis_even(N) :-\n    N > 0,\n    N1 is N - 1,\n    is_odd(N1).  % ← Chama is_odd\n\n% Caso base de is_odd\nis_odd(1).\n\n% is_odd recursivo: N é ímpar se N-1 é par\nis_odd(N) :-\n    N > 1,\n    N1 is N - 1,\n    is_even(N1).  % ← Chama is_even",
        "type": "code",
        "language": "prolog",
        "name": "",
        "lastOutput": "true.",
        "lastOutputHtml": "<pre class=\"text-result\" dir=\"ltr\">true.</pre>"
      },
      {
        "id": 34,
        "code": "### Testar em Prolog",
        "type": "markdown",
        "language": "markdown",
        "name": "",
        "lastOutput": "",
        "lastOutputHtml": ""
      },
      {
        "id": 35,
        "code": "% Testar par/ímpar\nis_even(0), writeln('✓ 0 is even').\nis_even(4), writeln('✓ 4 is even').\nis_odd(3), writeln('✓ 3 is odd').\nis_odd(7), writeln('✓ 7 is odd').",
        "type": "code",
        "language": "prolog",
        "name": "",
        "lastOutput": "✓ 0 is even\n✓ 4 is even\n✓ 3 is odd\n✓ 7 is odd",
        "lastOutputHtml": "<pre class=\"text-result\" dir=\"ltr\">✓ 0 is even\n✓ 4 is even\n✓ 3 is odd\n✓ 7 is odd</pre>"
      },
      {
        "id": 36,
        "code": "### Verificar Recursão Mútua",
        "type": "markdown",
        "language": "markdown",
        "name": "",
        "lastOutput": "",
